// Reviewer correction: an earlier version of this file wrongly claimed no
// primitive existed to deliver a restrain rider on a weapon strike. It does:
// `MeleeConstructor.damage_effect: Option<CombatEffect>` already attaches an
// arbitrary buff to a melee hit (see hammer/pile_driver.ron, which grants
// Rooted exactly this way). Ships as a direct touch-range `BasicMelee` --
// `Stab` maps to `DamageKind::Piercing` natively (common/src/comp/melee.rs),
// matching the sheet's own Piercing damage_type -- rather than the
// self-buff-triggers-on-next-hit framing the sheet literally describes (no
// existing pattern arms "your next weapon swing" with an arbitrary
// caster-agnostic melee_constructor; every *_smite.ron SelfBuff instead
// bakes its rider into a dedicated BuffKind, none of which is Rooted).
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 25,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 14, poise: 5, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        damage_effect: Some(Buff((
            kind: Rooted,
            dur_secs: 6.0,
            strength: Value(1.0),
            chance: 1.0,
        ))),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Conjuration), source: Some(Primordial)),
)
